126:One of the main purposes of research on design theory is to classify $t$-$(v,k,\lambda)$ designs, i.e., for given parameters $t$, $v$, $k$, and $\lambda$, construct the corresponding design, enumerate the possible constructions and determine the equivalence classes of $t$-$(v,k,\lambda)$ designs up to isomorphism, or show that no such design can exist. 
128:However, it remains an important open problem to provide explicit constructions.
131:We contribute to the construction of designs by proposing a new method of construction using square matrices satisfying certain algebraic conditions. 
133:Such matrices are known as \emph{weighing matrices} in the literature.
134:We will see that our method can also be applied to some variations of weighing matrices as well as to association schemes.
