-{"schema_version": 2, "model": "anthropic/claude-sonnet-5", "effort": "medium", "params": {"n": 37, "records": 12, "pool": 18}, "seed": 1467681363, "solved": "solved", "parsed": true, "verify_ok": true, "verify_reason": "ok", "reply": "Looking at this problem, I recognize that:\n\n1. Switching by e(x) (diagonal conjugation) doesn't change principal minors' determinants, and phi is a bijection on vertices \u2014 so the count of 4-blocks with a given determinant depends **only on q** (and its mod-4 class), not on the specific parameters u,t,switch_r,switch_s,switch_infinity.\n\n2. For q\u22611 mod 4 (symmetric conference matrix), analyzing the 4\u00d74 principal minors shows determinants only take values **{-3, 5}**, with exact counts:\n   - N(-3) = q(q-1)(q+1)(q-5)/96\n   - N(5) = q(q-1)\u00b2(q+1)/32\n\n3. For q\u22613 mod 4 (skew conference matrix), determinants only take values **{1, 9}**, with exact counts:\n   - N(9) = q(q-1)(q+1)\u00b2/96\n   - N(1) = q(q-1)(q+1)(q-3)/32\n\nApplying these formulas to each record's (q, target):\n\n- 0: q=101,target=5 \u2192 3,219,375\n- 1: q=79,target=9 \u2192 410,800\n- 2: q=59,target=1 \u2192 359,310\n- 3: q=41,target=-3 \u2192 25,830\n- 4: q=53,target=5 \u2192 241,839\n- 5: q=97,target=-3 \u2192 874,552\n- 6: q=67,target=9 \u2192 212,993\n- 7: q=107,target=1 \u2192 3,981,042\n- 8: q=83,target=9 \u2192 500,241\n- 9: q=47,target=9 \u2192 51,888\n- 10: q=73,target=-3 \u2192 275,502\n- 11: q=37,target=-3 \u2192 16,872\n\n<answer>[3219375, 410800, 359310, 25830, 241839, 874552, 212993, 3981042, 500241, 51888, 275502, 16872]</answer>", "error": null, "elapsed_sec": 231.13, "http_status": 200, "finish_reason": "stop", "preset": "hard", "escalation_round": 2}
