Thus, we can apply Theorem~\ref{thm:des}, to deduce that 
\begin{itemize}
    \item $\mathfrak H_{S}(4n+2,4,5)$ is a $3$-$(4n+2,4,3n)$ design;
    \item  $\mathfrak H_{S}(4n+2,4,-3)$ is a $3$-$(4n+2,4,n-1)$ design.
\end{itemize}
\end{example}

Due to the Paley digraph construction above, symmetric conference matrices of order $n$ are known to exist when $n = q+1$ and $q \equiv 1 \pmod 4$ is a prime power. See \cite{BS} for more constructions. 
