\subsection{2-designs from equiangular tight frames and Hadamard matrices}
In this subsection, we show how $2$-designs can be obtained from Seidel matrices with precisely two distinct eigenvalues and complex Hadamard matrices over the third roots of unity.
Seidel matrices having precisely two distinct eigenvalues are more commonly known as (real) \textbf{equiangular tight frames}.
See~\cite{etf} for an overview of equiangular tight frames.

