Set $X = \left [ \begin{smallmatrix}
    0 & 1 \\ 1 & 0
\end{smallmatrix} \right ]$ and $Y = \left [ \begin{smallmatrix}
    1 & 0 \\ 0 & -1
\end{smallmatrix} \right ]$.
For each binary vector $\mathbf k = (k_1,k_2,k_3,k_4,k_5,k_6) \in \{0,1\}^6$, define the matrix $T_{\mathbf k}$ as
\[
T_{\mathbf k} := X^{k_1}Y^{k_2} \otimes X^{k_3}Y^{k_4} \otimes X^{k_5}Y^{k_6}. 
\]
Set $\mathbf v = \frac{1}{2\sqrt{3}}(-1+2\sqrt{-1},1,1,1,1,1,1,1)$.
The lines spanned by the unit vectors $\mathbf v T_{\mathbf k}$ for $\mathbf k \in \{0,1\}^6$ are called \textbf{Hoggar's lines}~\cite{H,JW}.
Let $G$ be the Gram matrix of the vectors $\mathbf v T_{\mathbf k}$. 
