Throughout, for positive integers $v$ and $k$, define $[v]=\{1,\ldots,v\}$ and $\binom{[v]}{k}=\{\alpha \subset [v]  \; : \; |\alpha|=k\}$. 
Let $A$ be a $v\times v$ matrix whose rows and columns are indexed by $[v]$. 
