Implemented a native Track-B generator based on the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.17528), but it is not yet shippable because the mandatory oracle run was externally blocked.

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.17528/gen_2402_17528.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.17528/selftest_report.json) — all local G1–G9(c) gates pass
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.17528/README.md)
- [Blocker report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.17528/BLOCKED.md)
- [Partial script-owned transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.17528/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)

Key measurements:

- Structured guessing: 0/200,000; exact probability ≈ `2.82e-87`
- Four no-tool attacks: each 0/8
- Reference trace/Newton algorithm: 11,825,836 operations, 8.819489 s median
- Compact invariant route: 30 operations
- Answer: 115 characters, 6 atoms

The hardening loop recorded two valid oracle failures at `easy`, then OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded” before the required third attempt. Consequently, there is no hardness verdict and no hinted/placebo transcripts. Resume with a funded credential:

```bash
cd /home/gson/gvrepo/results/2402.17528
python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_2402_17528.py
```
